1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,850
I built an audio editor you talk to.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:09,250
Prepping one blend is a pile of small chores. Or just describe it.

3
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:13,060
You type the edit in plain English.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,950
The agent picks a tool, and runs it.

5
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:22,850
It flags a downbeat half a second into the file.

6
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:28,110
Then the blend: a crossfade, with a two kilohertz low-pass.

7
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:31,370
Have a listen.

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,630
Mastered to minus fourteen loofs, exported as a WAV.

9
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:49,590
The same recordings show an extended intro, and a three-track mini-mix.

10
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:57,990
Ninety-three tools run on your machine. Only the chat goes to your provider.

11
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:04,110
Limits: synthetic tracks, no stems, unsigned installers.

12
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:08,430
Free and open source. What would you hand off first?

